# rule|file|NaN|reason
# Used by scripts/style-check/style-check.ts. Keep the count exact: the check fails when it is too low as well.

# A Drop that runs while a panic unwinds must not panic: a second panic aborts the process.

# The guard of a test must survive a test that panicked, or it hides the failure that matters.

# The light-cycles example uses native generators, a nightly-only feature.

# A panic must not cross the C boundary: this is the defence in depth that the guide allows.

# The one catch_unwind outside the FFI boundary: the helper that the tests use to check a panic.

# anyhow_pub: a public signature returns anyhow. Exceptions: test and benchmark helpers behind a
# feature, not library API.

# glob: every glob import still to be replaced with explicit imports (tracker items G2 and G3). The rows go away with the fix.

# operator: an overload that has a math or logic meaning (U22). Each line names the meaning.

# pub_const_fn: a public const fn (U21). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# A hand-written Eq, Ord or PartialOrd: the compiler checks a derive, not a manual impl.

# assert_no_message: an assert with no message (P13). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# long_chain: a statement with five or more chained calls (P15). Each row is a count that may only go down.



# dyn_param: a public fn takes a trait object. Each row is a trait object that stays, with its reason.


# turbofish_collect_parse: a collect or parse turbofish (P2). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# untyped_long_chain_let: a let of a chain of five or more calls with no type (P5). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# pub_vec_return: a public function returns a Vec. The guide prefers an iterator. These keep a Vec:
# each one returns an owned byte buffer or an owned list that the caller keeps.

# pub_vec_param: a public function takes a Vec. The guide prefers impl IntoIterator when the function
# only iterates. These keep the list, sort it, or hand it on as an owned value.

# pub_impl_into: a public function takes impl Into<T>. A library may do so where call-site ergonomics
# matter most. These are the validating constructors that take a &str or a String, and the signaling
# builders that store an SDP string or a reason.

# crate_example: a library crate with no doc example (D2). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# self_convention: a by-value as_ or to_ method. Each type is Copy, so self by value is the right form.
# fn_import: a top-level function imported by its bare name (O23). Each row is a count that may only go down.



# abbrev_name: identifiers that are still letter-deleted abbreviations (ctx, addr, conn, msg, buf, opts, prev, ...).
# Each row goes down as the names are renamed; a new one fails the check. Reason: a follow-up rename of an existing name.




# trait_import_scope: a top-level `use ... as _;` (O22). Each row is a count that may only go down.



